(GOVERNMENT OF INDIA - MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE & FARMERS WELFARE) Tj
T*
(OPERATIONAL GUIDELINES: AGRICULTURE INFRASTRUCTURE FUND \(AIF\) / DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE / NABARD / COMMERCIAL BANKS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Overview & Objective:) Tj
T*
(Medium-long term debt financing facility for investment in viable projects) Tj
T*
(for post-harvest management infrastructure and community farming assets.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Eligibility Criteria:) Tj
T*
(1. Agri-entrepreneurs, Startups, Primary Agricultural Credit Societies) Tj
T*
(   \(PACS\), FPOs, SHGs, and MSMEs setting up post-harvest management) Tj
T*
(   facilities.) Tj
T*
(2. Eligible projects include cold chains, pack houses, silos,) Tj
T*
(   sorting/grading units, assaying units, and ripening chambers.) Tj
T*
(3. Borrower must have credit approval from participating lending) Tj
T*
(   institutions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Financial Assistance and Subsidy:) Tj
T*
(1. 3% interest subvention per annum on institutional loans up to Rs. 2 Crore) Tj
T*
(   for a maximum duration of 7 years, along with CGTMSE credit guarantee) Tj
T*
(   coverage fee paid by Government.) Tj
T*
(3. Maximum financial assistance cap is Rs 2.00 Crore per unit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Mandatory Documents Checklist:) Tj
T*
(1. Detailed Project Report \(DPR\) with civil and technical estimates) Tj
T*
(2. Land ownership title or registered long lease \(minimum 10 years\)) Tj
T*
(3. Bank sanction letter / application form) Tj
T*
(4. GST and Udyam Registration) Tj
T*
(5. Statutory approvals / clearances for civil construction) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Application Procedure:) Tj
T*
(1. Mode: Online via Agri Infra Portal) Tj
T*
(2. Official Portal: https://agriinfra.dac.gov.in/) Tj
T*
ET
